+# Full five-turn review obligations
+
+Source: complete Kędra contribution OWR3/2015 printed199–200, official https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46555 . Local sources/printed199.png is visually checked. Finite presentation and ordinary homogeneous quasimorphisms are essential; the later partial-quasimorphism duality is different. The original remains unsolved5/5.
+
+Audit every turn, including these risks:
+- Turn1: right-sided telescoping of noncommuting conjugation operators, combining image subgroups only inside an abelian kernel, finite normal generation of the class-two quotient's derived group, uniform constants and the real-homomorphism/torsion alternatives. Do not assume G' is finitely generated.
+- Turn2: finite-index core and Schreier hypotheses; restriction versus intrinsic norms; bounded-kernel lifting; transfer into a central finite-index subgroup and finite generation of its derived intersection.
+- Turn3: exact quotient M_Q×Q requires splitting. Finite generation of the coinvariant factor follows from the quotient, not finite generation of M. Both dichotomies pass via bounded kernel and product norms.
+- Turn4: the finite presentation is promised to have bounded derived subgroup; no recognition algorithm. Check integer lattice versus real span, rational denominator clearing, finite vertex enumeration and the primal-dual certificates, including rank defects and torsion.
+- Turn5: verify all finite-presentation relators map to B_{K+2} using δσ_iδ^{-1}=σ_{i+1} only in its valid nonwrap range. The exact primary homogeneous signature at σ_1^{-4}σ_2σ_1²σ_2 is -2 for every strand number≥3; see Brandenbursky–Kędra §4.8 printed2882–2883, sources/concordance.pdf and printed2883.png. This is an ordinary homogeneous detector with finite K-dependent defect, not a uniform-in-K claim. For the infinite presentation, H=<a_0,a_1> is an image of B3, w∈H', and t³ displaces all finite families of its conjugates. Apply BIP Theorem2.2(i), sources/bip2008.pdf printed14 and proof16–18, with the actual commutator length of w^n; bound42 is on the ambient normal word norm, not only commutator length. No claim about all elements of finite truncations or abstract non-finite-presentability of the limit.
+
+All raw primary PDFs and screenshots are local-only under /workspace/shared/math-30002762/sources. Their hashes are in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json and SOURCE_ADDITION_T5.json. Other primary URLs and credit are in SOURCE_GATE.md and TURN_5.md. The mathematical finite controls require only Python3 standard library. Run REPLAY_ALL.py; sources are optional and their actual check count is reported. All previous files must remain byte-identical; corrections, if required, are additive. Final remote head will be provided separately.
