+# Conjugation-invariant norm dichotomies: reviewed partial results
+
+**Original unsolved, five substantive turns completed.** The source seeks a finitely presented counterexample to bounded-versus-undistorted cyclic powers or bounded-versus-detection by an ordinary homogeneous quasimorphism. No counterexample or universal theorem for all finitely presented groups is supplied.
+
+Read FINAL_RESULT.md, the five turn proofs, and review/REVIEW.md. The valid partials exclude all finitely generated virtually metabelian groups and split abelian extensions of groups satisfying a dichotomy. They also give an exact rational stable-norm algorithm on a supplied bounded-derived-subgroup class, and an obstruction to a concrete finite braid-shift repair. The algorithm does not recognize its input hypothesis. All finite-index comparisons use ambient norms. Signature and displacement results are credited primary inputs; no novelty or human peer-review certification.
+
+All36 frozen author files and five manifest-bound review files are unchanged. The private working audit and raw source PDFs/screenshots are excluded. Fresh main and final author WIP ancestry are preserved. Only this target's QUEUE status/turn cells are changed to unsolved5/5.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+Python3 standard library suffices. Run from this directory:
+
+    python verify_publication.py
+
+This verifies the frozen author and review bindings, replays all345888 author and47964 independent assertions, and reports the actual optional source count. A public checkout without sources/ reports0 and does not claim primary PDF hash verification. To repeat all eight source bindings, populate sources/ with the files specified in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json and SOURCE_ADDITION_T5.json, using the primary URLs in the source gate and final review request. A partially populated directory fails. Finite controls supplement written proofs and cited theorems; they do not recompute knot signatures or certify infinite assertions by sampling.
